course: dictionary
lesson: 235
title: Allocate: sharing things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To allocate something is to give out a share of it to a person or for a purpose. When you decide who gets what, or what each part is for, you are allocating it. Other words for this are give out, share and set aside.
explain: «Ella uses three jars, SPEND, SAVE and GIVE, and splits her £6 into £2 for each.» Each jar gets a share of her money for a purpose: now, later or sharing. Sharing money out like this is called allocating.
explain: The same idea works with numbers in maths. «Allocate 30 pupils equally into 5 groups» means you share the 30 pupils out so every group gets the same amount, which is 6 in each. Check it: 6 × 5 = 30.
explain: Teachers allocate seats, tasks and time too. Allocate is a formal word, so you will meet it in school letters and in money or business writing. To check your meaning, swap in give out or share and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Allocate means to give out a share of something for a particular person or purpose.
fact: Allocate is a verb: allocate, allocates, allocated, allocating.
fact: You can allocate money, time, seats or tasks.
fact: Everyday words for allocate are give out, share and set aside.
fact: Formal writing often uses allocate where a speaker would say share.
exercise: «Ella splits her £6 into £2 for each jar.» What is she doing with her money? | Counting it twice | Losing it | Spending it all today | *Allocating it to three jars
exercise: «Allocate 30 pupils equally into 5 groups.» How many pupils go in each group? | 4 | 5 | 25 | *6
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to allocate? | Forget | Hide | Tangle | *Share
test: The teacher will allocate the tasks to each table. What does allocate mean here? | *To give out a share of the tasks | To finish the tasks | To hide the tasks | To ask for help with the tasks
test: Which is the past tense of allocate? | allocate | allocates | *allocated | allocating
exam: Ben has 24 stickers and allocates them equally to 4 friends. How many does each friend get? | 4 | *6 | 8 | 20
